            "visual_notes": "Open on a close-up of a single raindrop clinging to a leaf, backlit by the sun, sparkling. Smooth camera push into the drop as the narrator speaks — the drop becomes a sphere filling the frame. Cut to a macro simulation animation: a ray of white light enters a spherical drop, shown as a thin beam. Inside, the beam splits into a fan of colored rays — red, orange, yellow, green, blue, violet — all refracting and reflecting. Use slow-motion particles to represent photons. Then cut to a wide shot of an open field with a distant rainbow arcing over a valley, the ground wet from a just-passed shower. The camera pans slowly left to right, following the arc. Final shot: a person standing on a hill, looking toward the rainbow, and as they take a step forward, the rainbow seems to shift in the sky — a subtle dolly-out reveals the illusion. Soft, ambient sound — dripping water, distant thunder fading, a single bird call.",
